14:  * <p>Rows are stored as documents keyed by attachment, so a waveform is never shared between
15:  * attachments, and every read parses the persisted document again. Reading a row back is therefore
16:  * the same path the app takes when it reloads an attachment from the database, which keeps stored
17:  * bytes and their origin intact across a reload.
